  "public_messages": [
    "I’m using the installed OpenSocrates controller as requested, then I’ll inspect the source-room instructions, collect the frozen evidence, build the calculations/workbook/report/deck, and verify the rendered outputs and JSON contract.",
    "The task and tooling files are present and unchanged. The key judgment is a capital-allocation trade-off under hard caps (EUR450k capex, 7 FTE, max two hubs), so I’m treating source provenance, constraint separation, and switching conditions as first-class outputs while keeping the quantitative work reproducible.",
    "The frozen room is now saved under `evidence/raw` with SHA-256 hashes. Initial reconciliation found deliberate data issues: repeated order rows, higher-revision order corrections, repeated/higher-revision returns, an orphan return, a post-cutoff return, cancelled/test/future order rows, and zero-price shipments. I’m carrying each into explicit audit fields and quality notes rather than suppressing it.",
    "The core model now reconciles 1,254 eligible shipped orders across 72 country-month records and ranks CZE+ESP first among feasible alternatives on the policy’s base metric: EUR198,099 annual incremental contribution, EUR225,000 capex, five FTE, 1.14-year simple payback. The defined stress remains positive at EUR32,180, so I’m presenting it as a gated recommendation with POL+ESP and NLD+ESP as explicit alternatives, not as certainty.",
    "Completed the Meridian Parts expansion analysis.\n\nRecommendation: fund CZE + ESP with gated release — €225,000 capex, 5 FTE, €198,099 base annual incremental contribution, 1.14-year payback; defined stress remains positive at €32,180.\n\nDeliverables:\n\n- [Executive report PDF](<CELL>/workspace/deliverables/meridian_parts_executive_report.pdf)\n- [Board presentation PPTX](<CELL>/workspace/deliverables/meridian_parts_board_presentation.pptx)\n- [Analytical workbook XLSX](<CELL>/workspace/deliverables/meridian_parts_analysis.xlsx)\n- [metrics.json](<CELL>/workspace/deliverables/metrics.json)\n- [Reproducibility instructions](<CELL>/workspace/REPRODUCE.md)\n- [Verification record](<CELL>/workspace/deliverables/verification.md)\n\nVerification passed for reconciliations, source hashes, JSON structure, workbook, PDF, PPTX and charts. Material limitations are disclosed: synthetic hub assumptions, reference-rate FX, no causal demand evidence, and no live lane-cost or cash-settlement data.\n\nOpenSocrates grounding: trade-off-analysis@3"
  ],
